      "content": "To prepare your Linux environment for VortexScale, first download the latest `vortex-cli` binary directly from our internal release repository, ensuring you grab the Linux ARM64 or x86_64 version appropriate for your host system. Once downloaded, execute `chmod +x <path-to-binary>` to grant execute permissions, allowing the operating system to run your custom tool immediately. You should then append the directory containing the binary to your system's `PATH` by adding the export command to your `.bashrc` file so it is available globally across all future sessions without restarting the terminal. Finally, initialize the agent by running `vortex init` in your working directory, which will automatically create the necessary local configuration files and verify your network connectivity before spinning up the first cluster. This sequence ensures you have a hardened, secure foundation before attempting any complex resource orchestration.",
