      "content": "Before proceeding, ensure your system has bash as the default shell and sufficient disk space for cluster data, as these prerequisites prevent immediate session failures. Address common \"command not found\" errors by verifying the exact path of the downloaded binary in your `/opt` or `~/dist` directory before exporting it to `PATH`. If `chmod +x` fails with a \"permission denied\" error, it usually indicates the file is not in a drop-in directory, so verify file ownership. Finally, `vortex init` will fail if network latency exceeds the SDK's timeout, so allow the command 5 minutes to complete locally or check for firewall rules blocking internal proxy ports. This detailed scope ensures junior developers can self-heal their environment without waiting for support tickets.",
